          "title": "You'll want to know: હવા",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હવા — havā — \"air\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સવારે હવા ઠંડી હશે. — savāre havā ṭhanḍī haśe — \"The air will be cool in the morning.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હવા (havā) is a loan from Arabic hawā', \"air\", which reached Gujarati through Persian. Its Arabic root is h-w-y (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
